<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Adalbert of Pomerania</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1162">1162</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Adalbert of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pomerania">Pomerania</a> was the first <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> of Pomerania, appointed in 1140 with his seat at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wolin">Wolin</a>. A chaplain of Duke Bolesław III of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>, he had taken part in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/otto-of-bamberg">Otto of Bamberg</a>'s missions to convert the Pomeranians in the 1120s. The see he headed later moved to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kamien-pomorski">Cammin</a>.</p></div>
